e record <span>⌕</span></a></header><main id="main"><div class="atlas-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Overview</a><span aria-hidden="true">/</span><span aria-current="page">Evidence & open questions</span></div><div class="page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">Evidence & open questions</div><h1>What is established?<br>What still needs a test?</h1><p class="lede">Finite mathematical checks, constructor executions and physical measurements answer different questions. The programme has no promoted physical identification.</p></div><div class="status-strip"><div>Physical promotion <b>0</b></div><div>Independent review <b>Scope-specific / pending or HOLD</b></div></div><article class="claim" id="canonical-map-v01"><div class="eyebrow">20 October 2026 UTC · Canonical map and component test 0.1</div><h2>The apparatus map now fixes action, energy and time</h2><p>The scaled canonical theorem gives ordinary flux–charge pairs the required opposite matter brackets and reciprocal gauge dynamics. Sixty-four exact checks pass. CD-1 specifies one instrumented four-link diamond, independent coupling witnesses, known-source injection and two analytically discriminating fault controls.</p><p>Engineering gates are proposed and require actual calibration and non-constructor review. Physical promotion 0.</p><a class="text-link" href="/evidence/canonical-map/">Read theorem and closed-diamond test →</a></article><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">01</div><div><h2>Assess each result at its own level.</h2><div class="atlas-evidence-levels"><div><span>01 / Mathematics</span><h3>A declared finite object</h3><p>Exact algebra or a scoped proof on a specified carrier, metric and source convention.</p></div><div><span>02 / Computation</span><h3>A reproducible execution</h3><p>A frozen numerical or exact record with input hashes, tolerances and failure controls.</p></div><div><span>03 / Review</span><h3>An attributable challenge</h3><p>A non-constructor return bound to the exact claim or package, with its independence and scope.</p></div><div><span>04 / Correspondence</span><h3>An eligible physical test</h3><p>A calibrated map, units, uncertainty, baseline and a frozen independent acceptance rule.</p></div></div><p>The CRL-2 source proposal is preserved as a proposal. Publishing this hierarchy does not enact it or promote a scientific status.</p><div class="actions"><a class="text-link" href="/sources/?id=A21">Read the source proposal →</a><a class="text-link" href="/reconciliation/">Inspect source dispositions →</a></div></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">02</div><div><h2>Current programme boundaries.</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Programme</th><th>What the current record supports</th><th>What remains open</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Source, events and refinement</td><td>Conditional finite mechanisms, exact compatibility and nonselection results</td><td>Native source selection, preparation and a physical time/observable map</td></tr><tr id="observation-review-status"><td>Observation and estimation</td><td>Finite observability results and constructor certificates on declared records</td><td>Attributable external replay, uniform guarantees where claimed and physical metrology; review HOLD preserved</td></tr><tr><td>Action and stability</td><td>Declared action, scoped stability results and conditional preparation/error budgets</td><td>Realization and records meeting the complete experiment contract</td></tr><tr><td>Parity transport</td><td>Finite selected sector, typed transport identities and prospective numeric admission</td><td>Non-constructor review of the new contract, original attributable approval/raw output gaps and physical parity</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="actions"><a class="text-link" href="/research/">Read the programme map →</a><a class="text-link" href="/research-record/">Inspect the source-bound returns →</a></div></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">03</div><div><h2>A concrete bridge candidate, with a data boundary.</h2><div id="measurable-audit-v01"><p>A rank-one rotor–matter circuit emulator was selected for development. The published LC device is a partial benchmark: its oscillator links and chain do not implement the full UD Hamiltonian and required diamonds.</p><p>No audited dataset supplies every preparation, energy and source-work gate. The next proposed component experiment is a closed-diamond test with a calibrated measurement contract.</p><div class="atlas-grid"><a class="atlas-card" href="/evidence/measurable-audit/"><h3>Read the realization and dataset audit</h3><p>Selection, inspected records, mismatches and minimum experiment requirements.</p><span class="card-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">04</div><div><h2>Read historical replication claims with their receipts.</h2><p>The historical parity record reports 12 in-scope passes and six failing controls from external-AI replication, with the permanent rider <em>transport consistency, not dynamical discovery</em>. Receipt linkage and the full ruling document are recovered; named or signed original approval and the raw-output commitment remain unresolved.</p><p>This is a source-recorded internal transport result. It is not independent-human review or a laboratory measurement, and the new prospective contract does not retroactively revise the old scores.</p><div class="actions"><a class="text-link" href="/research/parity/">Read the parity programme →</a><a class="text-link" href="/research-record/#custody">Inspect source and review custody →</a></div></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">05</div><div><h2>What a physical return must contain.</h2><ol class="atlas-sequence"><li><strong>State the correspondence.</strong><span>Define the mathematical object, measured observable, units and calibration.</span></li><li><strong>Freeze the test.</strong><span>Specify baseline, exclusions, uncertainty budget, acceptance and failure rules before target exposure.</span></li><li><strong>Separate the evaluation.</strong><span>Record target custody, reviewer independence, negative results and the exact supported scope.</span></li></ol><div class="actions"><a class="text-link" href="/contribution/">Choose a review or experiment gate →</a><a class="text-link" href="/archive/">Find the underlying evidence →</a></div></div></section><section class="chapter"><div class="chapter-label">06</div><div><h2>Applied programmes have separate evidence ledgers.</h2><div class="atlas-grid"><a class="atlas-card" href="https://mqm-research.ben-w-mayes.chatgpt.site/"><h3>MQM</h3><p>Fault-aware quantum-code and controller research; hardware advantage needs its own evidence.</p><span class="card-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="atlas-card" href="https://voxifold-systems.ben-w-mayes.chatgpt.site/"><h3>Lattix Systems</h3><p>Spatial compute; equal-recall, equal-hardware benchmarks remain separate.</p><span class="card-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></div></section><span id="research-record-extension"></span></main><footer><div><a href="/">Unified Dynamics</a><p>Benjamin Walker Mayes · Independent researcher<br>AI-assisted research · Public atlas</p></div><div><a href="/sources/">Sources & coverage</a><a href="/contribution/">Contribution</a><a href="https://tetrahedral-packet-complexes.ben-w-mayes.chatgpt.site/">Living research portal ↗</a></div><p class="footer-rule">Proof, simulation and physical correspondence retain distinct evidence status. Physical promotion: 0.</p></footer></div></body></html>
